<title>FINLAND: ICE HOCKEY-REVISED WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP SCHEDULE.</title>
<headline>ICE HOCKEY-REVISED WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP SCHEDULE.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Revised schedule in the ice</p>
<p>hockey world championship following a switch in the order of the</p>
<p>April 28 Group A matches (times GMT):</p>
<p>Group A (in Helsinki):</p>
<p>April 26 1300  Czech Republic v Germany</p>
<p>	    1700  Finland v France</p>
<p>April 27 1300  Russia v Slovakia</p>
<p>	    1700  Finland v Czech Republic</p>
<p>April 28 1300  Germany  v Russia</p>
<p>	    1700  Slovakia vs France</p>
<p>April 29 1600  Germany v Finland</p>
<p>April 30 1300  Russia v France</p>
<p>	    1700  Czech Republic v Slovakia</p>
<p> May 1    1600  Czech Republic v Russia</p>
<p> May 2    1300  France v Germany</p>
<p>	    1700  Finland v Slovakia</p>
<p> May 3    1000  France v Czech Republic</p>
<p>	    1330  Slovakia v Germany</p>
<p>	    1700  Russia v Finland</p>
<p>Group B (in Turku):</p>
<p>April 26 1200  Canada v Norway</p>
<p>	    1600  Sweden v Italy</p>
<p>April 27 1200  U.S. v Latvia</p>
<p>	    1600  Sweden v Canada</p>
<p>April 28 1200  Latvia v Italy</p>
<p>	    1600  Norway v U.S.</p>
<p>April 29 1530  Norway v Sweden</p>
<p>April 30 1200  U.S. v Italy</p>
<p>	    1600  Canada v Latvia</p>
<p> May 1    1530  Canada v U.S.</p>
<p> May 2    1200  Italy v Norway</p>
<p>	    1600  Sweden v Latvia</p>
<p> May 3    1000  Italy v Canada</p>
<p>	    1330  U.S. v Sweden</p>
<p>	    1700  Latvia v Norway</p>
<p>Finals, top three teams from groups A and B (in Helsinki):</p>
<p> May 5    1300  Winner Group A (A1) v Third Group B (B3)</p>
<p>	    1700  B1 v A3</p>
<p> May 6    1300  A2 v B2</p>
<p>	    1700  A3 v B3</p>
<p> May 7    1300  B2 v A1</p>
<p>	    1700  B1 v A2</p>
<p> May 8    1600  A1 v B1</p>
<p> May 9    1300  B2 v A3</p>
<p>	    1700  B3 v A2</p>
<p> May 10   1300  Third place match</p>
<p> May 11   1300  1st final (best of three)</p>
<p> May 13   1600  2nd final</p>
<p> May 14   1600  3rd final (if necessary)</p>
<p>Relegation play-offs (in Tampere):</p>
<p> May 6    1300  Fourth Group A (A4) v Sixth Group B (B6)</p>
<p>	    1600  B4 v A6</p>
<p> May 7    1300  B6 v A5</p>
<p>	    1600  B5 v A6</p>
<p> May 8    1300  B5 v A4</p>
<p>	    1600  B4 v A5</p>
<p> May 9    1530  A6 v B6</p>
<p> May 10   1300  A4 v B4</p>
<p>	    1600  A5 v B5</p>
<p>Last team relegated to regional play-offs for berth in</p>
<p>enlarged pool A world championship in Switzerland in 1998.</p>
</text>
